    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p81-q55-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Write down the domain of $f$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(-\\infty,2)\\cup(2,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "The denominator is zero at $x=2$, so this value is excluded.\n\n$$\\operatorname{dom}f=(-\\infty,2)\\cup(2,\\infty).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p81-q55-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Sketch the graph of $y=f(x)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p81-q55-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Positive cubic ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=(x+2)(x-1)(x+1),\\quad x\\ne2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", crossing the axes at ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(-2,0),\\ (-1,0),\\ (1,0)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(0,-2)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", with an open circle at ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "(2,12)",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p81-q55-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cancel the factor ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x-2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " while retaining the original exclusion ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "x\\ne2",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For $x\\ne2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}f(x)&=\\frac{(x^2-1)(x^2-4)}{x-2}\\\\f(x)&=\\frac{(x-1)(x+1)(x-2)(x+2)}{x-2}\\\\f(x)&=(x+2)(x-1)(x+1).\\end{align*}$$\nThe single roots are $x=-2$, $x=-1$ and $x=1$, so the graph crosses the $x$-axis at each of these values.\n$$\\begin{align*}f(0)&=2(-1)(1)\\\\f(0)&=-2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe leading coefficient is positive, so the left end points downwards and the right end points upwards.\n\nAt the excluded value $x=2$, the simplified cubic has height\n$$\\begin{align*}y_{\\text{hole}}&=(2+2)(2-1)(2+1)\\\\y_{\\text{hole}}&=12.\\end{align*}$$\nDraw an open circle at $(2,12)$. The graph has a hole there; $x=2$ is not a vertical asymptote.",
