                "description": "An ungridded positive cubic with three single roots, a negative y-intercept and a labelled open circle on its upper right branch.",
                "mathematics": "Plot y=(x+2)(x-1)(x+1) for x≠2. Crossings are x=-2,-1,1; the y-intercept is -2. Remove the point (2,12). Preserve positive cubic end behaviour without requiring turning-point coordinates.",
